feat: Tier 0 redesign — slime farm bootstrap, no sieving

Replaces the sieving-based Tier 0 (Sky-Bees-Reborn-era pattern) with a
slime-farm bootstrap. Detailed rationale in docs/backlog.md "Recently
moved out of backlog" and project memory file.

Design summary:

- Player spawns with minimal kit (2-3 saplings + water bucket + lava
  bucket + ~16 cooked beef). FTB Quests book auto-opens.
- Vanilla cobble generator from the buckets.
- Second water source via Ex Deorum rain-collection barrel placed
  outside the Skyblock Builder claim.
- Dark-room mob farm built from cobble.
- Vanilla minecraft:slime spawns via KubeJS-overridden spawn rules
  (drops slime-chunk + swamp-biome requirements). Vanilla slime is
  the Metallic parent per PF's ParentSpeciesEntry.
- Welcome quest chapter (~18 quests) rewards 2x Metallic Frogspawn
  at completion. Two for a breeding pair from minute one.
- First Iron Configurable Froglight is the first iron source.

Recovery design:

- Cooldown-repeatable "Replacement Frogspawn" quest in Welcome chapter
  (1h cooldown, 4 slimeballs cost, 2x Metallic Frogspawn reward).
  Handles frogs dying / jumping off the island.

Pack changes:

- packwiz remove rain-shield (conflicted with rain-collection barrel
  inside the player's claim).
- Pack version bump to 0.0.4 to reflect the design pivot.

